        {
          "id": "/page/10/SectionHeader/1",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h2>Veal chops with caraway seeds - Teleci žebirka na kminë</h2>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              355.5,
              195.75
            ],
            [
              1140.0,
              195.75
            ],
            [
              1140.0,
              261.0
            ],
            [
              355.5,
              261.0
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            355.5,
            195.75,
            1140.0,
            261.0
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/10/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/10/ListGroup/2",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<ul style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<li>• 6 veal chops</li>\n<li>• 1/2 cup flour</li>\n<li>• 1/2 cup vegetable oil</li>\n<li>• 2 tablespoons butter</li>\n<li>• 1 cup chicken stock</li>\n<li>• 1 small onion</li>\n<li>• 1 teaspoon caraway seeds</li>\n<li>• salt</li>\n</ul>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              124.5,
              246.375
            ],
            [
              417.0,
              246.375
            ],
            [
              417.0,
              448.875
            ],
            [
              124.5,
              448.875
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            124.5,
            246.375,
            417.0,
            448.875
          ],
          "children": [],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/10/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/10/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Pound the veal chops lightly-they should not be more than 1/2\" thick. Make a few short cuts on the edges to prevent curling, salt them on both sides, and dust with flour on one side. Brown chops in hot oil on both sides, floured side first. In a skillet combine the butter and finely chopped onion and set over medium heat.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              570.0,
              259.875
            ],
            [
              1351.5,
              259.875
            ],
            [
              1351.5,
              421.875
            ],
            [
              570.0,
              421.875
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            570.0,
            259.875,
            1351.5,
            421.875
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/10/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/10/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When the onion becomes translucent add the caraway seeds, some of the chicken stock and the veal chops and simmer about 30 minutes or until the chops are tender.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              570.0,
              407.25
            ],
            [
              1341.0,
              407.25
            ],
            [
              1341.0,
              504.0
            ],
            [
              570.0,
              504.0
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            570.0,
            407.25,
            1341.0,
            504.0
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/10/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/10/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Remove the veal chops. Bring the liquid to boil, blend in flour and remaining stock, and boil until the sauce thickens (about 5 minutes). Strain the sauce over the veal chops, simmer 5 minutes. Serve with noodles, rice, salad.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              570.0,
              493.875
            ],
            [
              1347.0,
              493.875
            ],
            [
              1347.0,
              616.5000000000001
            ],
            [
              570.0,
              616.5000000000001
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
